    "result_text": "All 51 tests pass, `BUILD SUCCESS`. The change is complete.\n\n## What I did\n\nThe `Owner` response is a MapStruct-mapped `OwnerDto` generated from `openapi.yml`. The stored `telephone` is already normalized to E.164 by `ValidateOwnerFields` (e.g. `0412 345 678` \u2192 `+61412345678`). I added a derived, read-only companion field without touching the raw value:\n\n1. **`src/main/resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 added a `telephoneDisplay` read-only string property to the `Owner` schema (next to the other derived fields like `contactPreference`), so the generated `OwnerDto` gains the field.\n\n2. **`OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 added `@Mapping(target = \"telephoneDisplay\", expression = \"java(telephoneDisplay(owner))\")` and a `telephoneDisplay(Owner)` helper that:\n   - splits the E.164 country code (`+61` \u2192 2 digits, `+1` \u2192 1 digit, mirroring the country codes the existing normalizer recognizes),\n   - groups the national digits left-to-right in threes,\n   - formats as `+<cc> <grouped national>` (\u2192 `+61 412 345 678`),\n   - returns `null` for an absent or non-E.164 value, leaving raw `telephone` untouched.\n\nThe Cp37 test now sees `telephone` = `+61412345678` (raw E.164) and `telephoneDisplay` = `+61 412 345 678`, and the full suite (51 tests) stays green.",
